		// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
		// The players' classes
		// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
		// Survival's own copies of the insurgent classes, under their own names so that checkpoint's
		// insurgent bots - which use the originals - are untouched. Each is the original copied verbatim
		// with four changes:
		//
		// - buy_order is knife and pistol only, both free. A run starts on 2 supply and the kit is
		//   bought up from there as it is earned (prices are in the generated block at the bottom).
		//   This cannot be done as an override of the original template: #base merging appends every
		//   inherited child whose NAME the override lacks, so a buy_order declaring only "weapon"
		//   entries would get the original's "gear" and "weapon_upgrade" entries merged back in.
		//
		// - ins_nightvision is in allowed_items, as sec_nightvision is for security's classes
		//   (theater_tug_nvg_default.theater), so NVG can be bought on any map. Its price and the
		//   unconditional definition are in the generated block, along with the slings.
		//
		// - weapon_m18_ins, the pink smoke that calls FireSupport's insurgent rocket strike, is in
		//   allowed_items for every class, not just the two specialists that carry it in checkpoint. It
		//   is priced high in the generated block.
		//
		// - weapon_healthkit is in allowed_items. Survival's insurgent squads have no medic class, so
		//   without it nobody on the players' team could heal. bm2_respawn does the healing: drop the
		//   pack, hold the knife, and it heals you up to the non-medic cap. The medpack is
		//   class_restricted, so it has to be listed per class; theater_tug_nvg_default.theater
		//   restates its definition with insurgents allowed.
		//
		// Because these are copies, a change to the originals (theater_tug_nvg_default.theater for the
		// tugvar classes, TUG's medicbomber_12p theater for the bomber) has to be repeated here.
		//
		// New names also start everyone with no saved loadout here: LoadoutSaverSlots keys saved
		// loadouts by class template, so a checkpoint loadout cannot come back at checkpoint prices.

